      "headline": {
        "en": "NAIC defends insurance oversight as Warren presses on private credit ties",
        "zh": "NAIC为保险业监管辩护，沃伦就私募信贷关联施压"
      },
      "summary": {
        "en": "The National Association of Insurance Commissioners defended US state insurance regulation in a response to Senator Elizabeth Warren, who raised concerns about insurers' growing ties to private investment firms and private credit exposure. The NAIC said it has strengthened asset-adequacy testing, introduced a 45 per cent risk-based capital charge for residual interests in structured securities, and added a process to assess credit rating providers' methodologies. Insurer exposure to private credit more than doubled over the past decade, from $386bn in 2014 to $849bn in 2024.",
        "zh": "美国全国保险监督官协会（NAIC）在回应参议员伊丽莎白·沃伦时，为美国州级保险监管作出辩护；沃伦对保险公司与私人投资公司日益紧密的关联及私募信贷敞口提出担忧。NAIC表示已加强资产充足性测试，对结构性证券的剩余权益引入45%的风险资本计提，并新增程序以评估信用评级机构的方法论与评级映射是否仍适用于监管目的。过去十年，保险公司对私募信贷的敞口增加逾一倍，从2014年的3860亿美元升至2024年的8490亿美元。"
      },
